  "worked_solution": "By the multiplication law for conditional probability, the required conditional probability is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(2\\le Y\\le 6\\,|\\,X=2) & =\\frac{P((2\\le Y\\le 6),X=2)}{P(X=2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{P(X=2,(2\\le Y\\le 6))}{P(X=2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{P(X=2,Y=2)+P(X=2,Y=4)+P(X=2,Y=6)}{P(X=2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{f(2,2)+f(2,4)+f(2,6)}{{f}_{X}(2)},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $f(x,y)$ is the joint probability mass function of $X$ and $Y,$ and ${f}_{X}(x)$ is the marginal distribution of $X.$\n\nRecall that the marginal distribution for $X$ corresponds to the row totals. Thus,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{X}(2) & =f(2,0)+f(2,2)+f(2,4)+f(2,6) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}+\\frac{1}{18}+0+\\frac{1}{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the given table, we have that $f(2,2)=\\frac{1}{18},f(2,4)=0$ and $f(2,6)=\\frac{1}{6}.$ \n\nFinally, substituting our values into our formula above, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(2\\le Y\\le 6\\,|\\,X=2) & =\\frac{f(2,2)+f(2,4)+f(2,6)}{{f}_{X}(2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{1}{18}+0+\\frac{1}{6})}{(\\frac{1}{3})} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{2}{9})}{(\\frac{1}{3})} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
